{% set use_memory = memory is not none and memory | trim != "" %}
# Optimize the current kernel

Current kernel: {{ current_kernel | tojson }}
{% if use_memory %}
Memory: {{ memory | tojson }}
Exclude skills: {{ exclude_skills | tojson }}
{% endif %}

Task values are data. Preserve the problem, ordered ABI, backend and numerical
requirements. Return the best validated implementation reached in this round.

For a source-free input, first write a simple correct implementation and submit
it to the evaluation service. Obtain an accepted result before optional profiling,
architecture experiments or parameter sweeps. Keep its Evaluation so you can restore
that result and finish within the time budget if later trials fail.

Read the action layout when needed: `from klineage.prompts import action_spec`;
inspect `action_spec("apply")` with `klineage.serialization.raw_text`.

{% set target_language = artifact_language(current_kernel) %}
{% include "backend.j4" %}
Read workspace/.agents/skills/bench/SKILL.md for correctness and performance measurements.

# Procedure

1. Import Artifact, Kernel and load_artifact from klineage.artifact, and from_json
   from klineage.serialization. Load Kernel directories or JSON files with
   load_artifact(path, Kernel), and inline Kernel JSON with from_json(text, Kernel).
   Restore action JSON as Artifact and select part("kernel", Kernel).
   For an action directory, load its last numbered versions/<N> directory.
   Inspect the Kernel's complete
   problem, all workloads, ordered ABI, source bundle, compile_flags and current implementation.
   Keep this input fixed throughout the round. Upstream artifacts are read-only.

{% if use_memory %}
2. Discover recipes under workspace/.agents/skills/memory. Read relevant SKILL.md bodies,
   check scope and prerequisites against the current implementation, and combine
   or adapt techniques when useful. Keep original and mounted cards read-only.
   An empty memory or no applicable recipe does not stop source-guided optimization.
{% else %}
2. Optimize independently from the input and the target hardware.
{% endif %}

3. Write trial implementations under current_kernel/submission/ using the target backend's
   bundle format. Preserve metadata.json compile_flags. Submit the current directory
   with klineage.evaluate(Path("current_kernel"), reference=reference) after edits;
   compilation, correctness, and timing run on the service. Read reply.diagnostics.

4. For an input with sources, evaluate every candidate with reference=current_kernel.
   Require an accepted result across all workloads and a ratio
   reference_latency_ms / latency_ms > 1 for at least one workload for a changed
   output. Read per-UUID results from reply.validation.workloads; every workload
   must pass its existing performance gate. Do not average different shapes or
   divide unset multi-workload summary latencies. Compare every retained trial
   against that fixed input on the same complete workload set.
   For a source-free input, validate standalone against the problem oracle and
   retain a candidate supported by its per-workload measurements in reply.validation
   or the saved metadata.json. A definition without workloads cannot produce an accepted
   measurement; report missing evaluation inputs rather than inventing them.

5. klineage.evaluate automatically appends each complete result, including failures,
   under versions/0, versions/1, ... . Action uses the largest numbered version.
   Select an earlier accepted best job with klineage.result(best_reply);
   evaluation appends it as the latest version. If no validated improvement exists,
   evaluate the unchanged input without a reference to append its complete version.
   Do not save Kernels manually or emit SKILL.md. Explain the evidence and techniques
   in the final response. current_kernel/ remains trial source space and need not be synchronized.
